[{"id":"VRCE-4-55-1","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":55,"verse":1,"english":"When the monkeys had been seated in that mountain, with the intention of putting a period to their existence through fasting a king of vultures happened to come to that quarter. And that long-lived bird was named Sampāti, the beautiful brother of Jaţāyu, famous for his strength and prowess.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-56-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4055001","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"50ecf59c6f301e96e3c7d4714cbb63a78aa4b48c59c3b4f946f73a9a4a6d61e1","compact":"a4500267960ee6be883866754eaf23a0378314c8c9663418c151de18c4d397ea","nasal":"a4500267960ee6be883866754eaf23a0378314c8c9663418c151de18c4d397ea"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-55-2","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":55,"verse":2,"english":"When the monkeys had been seated in that mountain, with the intention of putting a period to their existence through fasting a king of vultures happened to come to that quarter. And that long-lived bird was named Sampāti, the beautiful brother of Jaţāyu, famous for his strength and prowess.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.815,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-56-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4055002","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"69736c0e836681ae7725a387a2ac59eb071e75810d315dd92399d849fcbb4abc","compact":"fdc34f1082698e8ed8d2f7d957b7e7771b6d5a209c673b5b1abb4c7651ace042","nasal":"3ae990c47ebb0b4cf9064a8619df3f34eb62165d51e69e4ccec8f1152b26046e"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-55-3","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":55,"verse":3,"english":"Issuing from a cavern of the mighty mountain Vindhya, he, seeing the monkeys seated, well pleased, said.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-56-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4055003","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0ed7319814547eec1087d4296972a2026da20ed8baeb3fb53831d5756bc984f6","compact":"b29b1f3ee122dde1a2faa6fecbe02ba844bf0b0cde391c7896bf2c5502f75bed","nasal":"6fca614d8c000be891c1783037dce57ee86f9540b52ec29f0595b750cb0db631"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-55-4","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":55,"verse":4,"english":"Verily man reapeth the fruit of his former acts; and therefore it is that this food ordained to that end, comes to me after a long time. I shall feed on these monkeys, one by one, slaying them one after another. Eyeing those apes, the bird expressed himself thus.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-56-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4055004","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f94eff8e0877ae5e3339d95346d7df7f6363cf73bec123581e81f172cc048f0f","compact":"0e72f394019691bd6c61202dea70a2b85b76d5c6f3680262c35d06d08acad0c3","nasal":"0e72f394019691bd6c61202dea70a2b85b76d5c6f3680262c35d06d08acad0c3"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-55-5","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":55,"verse":5,"english":"Verily man reapeth the fruit of his former acts; and therefore it is that this food ordained to that end, comes to me after a long time. I shall feed on these monkeys, one by one, slaying them one after another. Eyeing those apes, the bird expressed himself thus.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.776,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-56-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4055005","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ada875f442bd85c23b3c447b640e8200b4eb9ad296884db2ad193ca96a201eea","compact":"ccd295a3f9a94a410a55966c790db56a04afadbf70f5f295cabfe25