t in Janasthāna. And how could Dasaratha, whose beloved eldest son is Rāma, dear to his superiors, be the friend of my brother?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.885,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-56-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4055019","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5e928a6967dbcc7b93fa893d39fbbe0e7ac9c1d31f8ee1cc94192fb1857de2c4","compact":"14b1f1e3f7e51100c889fb89281fdeb48c8f0b952ab1c82a5d9b1e9da0d744bf","nasal":"14b1f1e3f7e51100c889fb89281fdeb48c8f0b952ab1c82a5d9b1e9da0d744bf"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-55-20","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":55,"verse":20,"english":"I wish to alight from this mountain-fastness. I have been well pleased by listening after a long time to the celebration of the virtues of my younger brother, cognizant of qualities and worthy of being extolled by reason of his prowess. You foremost of monkeys, I wish to hear of the destruction of Jaţāyu, who dwelt in Janasthāna. And how could Dasaratha, whose beloved eldest son is Rāma, dear to his superiors, be the friend of my brother?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-56-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4055020","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"82a86a404d47ac5b7b461932f776749b004e497e981c01a563010aba98426ab2","compact":"9e41375b2bd6a0893724af7eb47ab1b446bd7e4a5390be46698437f1a52acd96","nasal":"9e41375b2bd6a0893724af7eb47ab1b446bd7e4a5390be46698437f1a52acd96"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-55-21","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":55,"verse":21,"english":"I can not move in consequence of my wings having been burnt by the solar rays. But I wish that you may take me down from this mountain.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.75,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-56-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4055021","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bf4e2227ea07c74da3c6e6a4108f5633704005225316b713bfcd79742e6570fa","compact":"f22b16b841cea3a0870d50791db58d8dcb014720c2152f774994387e7338e822","nasal":"fc8a84164fee8b46e8031c006ab856af4345f32177c7c2843bd3ac68e8fb4b87"}}]
